  "authoringNote": "No order receipt record is supplied, as the manifest scenario states, so no current usable receipt and no receipt candidate exists (C09). R05 is missing for the authorization coordinator with only R05.no_usable_receipt, which names no document. R05.order_receipt_missing is not added: that key concerns a usable receipt that fails to link to the order, and no receipt exists here. R05.no_usable_order does not hold because the final order f26a-order v1 is current and usable. R05 still cites the order date, the only stated R05 evidence field (C05); the null order time supplies no fact. R02 passes citing the beneficiary name and identifier of the encounter and the order only (four). R04 passes citing the encounter status, date and practitioner identifier and the order status, date and practitioner identifier (six; the null completion and order times supply no fact). The rest follows the supported packet, checked by hand: the final encounter (2026-08-26) and the final signed order (2026-09-04) both name practitioner identifier SYN-PRAC-0001; the order is after the encounter, on a different date, and within the inclusive C01 bound 2027-02-26; the order item code K0823 equals the case; the named supplier record f26a-supplier-status v1 is usable and states non_exempt, established, no new enrollment, no ownership change and the interval 2026-01-01 to 2026-12-31, which contains the assessment date 2026-10-18. R01 passes citing the seven supplier record facts and the order item code; R03 passes citing the nine order facts. R06 stays manual_review for the qualified clinical reviewer with R06.clinical_review and the five full /clinical/ pointers; it neither blocks nor satisfies readiness and draws no medical necessity conclusion. R07 passes citing the stated LCMP flag false (the null evaluation date supplies no fact); no ATP, specialty, home assessment or proof-of-delivery item is required. R08 passes on the reviewed pack and the supported date. R10 is not_applicable with R10.pure_assessment. clinicalReviewRequired is true. R09 passes: every supplied version is available, hash-valid, application/json, a valid body of its metadata kind and bound to the case. The state is needs_information from R05 alone. Quarantine and superseded lists are empty, and every parent affectedDocuments set is empty because no held condition is restricted, unreadable or failed provenance (C07). The absent receipt makes no delivery claim and no clinical assertion.",
